{
  "dom_id": "questionContainer",
  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "If a circle represents a whole, which model shows $210%?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, recall that $210%$ is the same as $\\frac{210}{100}.$\n\nWe now need to simplify this fraction. Dividing the numerator and denominator by $10,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{210}{100}=\\frac{210÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{21}{10}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write $\\frac{21}{10}$ as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{21}{10}=2\\,\\text{R}\\,1=2\\,\\frac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nThe model that shows $2\\,\\frac{1}{10}$ is:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14128162/assets/b901819e40d67559b5b8f6d137ab5595531801f5529f778be34c768b2dc40c3f.png)",
